<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Document</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 {
            font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif;
        }
        table {
            width: 100%;
            border-collapse: collapse;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        td, th {
            padding: 8px;
            text-align: left;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
        }
        .header-info {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .contact-info {
            font-size: 0.9em;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 3em; margin: 0;">UAH</h1>
            <p style="margin: 5px 0;">The University of Alabama in Huntsville</p>
            <p style="margin: 5px 0;">Office of the Vice President and Chief of Staff</p>
        </div>

        <div class="header-info">
            <div class="contact-info">
                <p>Phone: {{ contact_phone }}</p>
                <p>FAX: {{ contact_fax }}</p>
                <p>Email: {{ contact_email }}</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 10px;">{{ date }}</p>

        <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">MEMORANDUM</h2>

        <p>TO: <span data-field="recipient.name">{{ recipient.name }}</span></p>
        <p>FROM: <span data-field="sender.name">{{ sender.name }}</span></p>
        <p>RE: <span data-field="subject">{{ subject }}</span></p>

        <p>I am writing to clarify how the research incentive pay for tenured and tenure-track faculty has been calculated historically at UAHuntsville. I have read several memoranda (from <span data-field="historical_person_1">{{ historical_person_1 }}</span> and some of the Provost's) dating back to {{ historical_year }} when the practice was initiated. I have also met with <span data-field="historical_person_2">{{ historical_person_2 }}</span> to determine how actually calculates research incentives for faculty. Several modifications were made after {{ modification_year }}, including increasing the maximum research incentive that a faculty member could receive to {{ percentage_1 }}% of the 9-month base salary and making adjustments for the transition from the quarter system to the semester system. Please understand that this practice was in place long before I came to UAHuntsville, and it did not change during my tenure. This memo is intended to describe (as simply as possible) how the research incentive pay is handled and not intended to justify the practice.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Typical Faculty Workload</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th></th>
                    <th></th>
                    <th></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Course 1 (3-Credit Hours)</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_1 }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_1_desc }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Course 2 (3-Credit Hours)</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_2 }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_2_desc }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Course 3 (3-Credit Hours)</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_3 }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_course_3_desc }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Research/Scholarly Work</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_research }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_research_desc }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Service</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_service }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ workload_service_desc }}</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>If a faculty member is working with Ph.D. students, then supervision of these students and their research counts for approximately one of the 3-credit hour courses.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Faculty Supervising Ph.D. Students</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th></th>
                    <th></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td>Course 1 (3-Credit Hours)</td>
                    <td>{{ supervision_course_1 }}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Course 2 (3-Credit Hours)</td>
                    <td>{{ supervision_course_2 }}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Supervising Ph.D. Students</td>
                    <td>{{ supervision_phd }}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Research/Scholarly Work</td>
                    <td>{{ supervision_research }}%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Service</td>
                    <td>{{ supervision_service }}%</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Since {{ year_since_1992 }} faculty who receive extramural funding for their research have been eligible for research incentive pay (from institutional funds) according to the amount of their allocated time for which they buy-out during the 9-month academic year. First I will describe the practice and process that is used to determine research incentive pay, and then will follow with a few examples.</p>

        <ol>
            <li>The buy-out of the first {{ percentage_buyout_1 }}% of a faculty member's time is applied to the Research/Scholarly Work component of their workload. That is, the faculty member is buying-out the {{ percentage_buyout_1 }}% of his/her salary that was committed to Research/Scholarly Work from institutional sources.
                <ul>
                    <li>Faculty who buy-out the first {{ percentage_buyout_1 }}% of their time receive research incentive pay of {{ incentive_pay_1 }}% of their 9-month academic year salary from institutional sources. For buy-outs of &lt;{{ threshold_1 }}% the formula used to calculate the incentive pay is</li>
                    <li>(X%)(0.35) = Incentive Pay%</li>
                    <li>where X is the % buyout that is &lt;{{ threshold_1 }}%.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Faculty who buy-out the first {{ percentage_buyout_2 }}% of their time do not get a reduction in their teaching load because they are buying out only their time committed to Research/Scholarly Work.</li>
        </ol>

        <p>2) Faculty who buy-out more than {{ percentage_buyout_2 }}% of their time receive additional research incentive pay. Those who buy-out an additional {{ percentage_buyout_3 }}% (50% total buyout) of their time receive an additional research incentive pay of {{ incentive_pay_2 }}% of their 9-month salary from institutional sources (14% total). For buy-outs of &gt;{{ threshold_2 }}% the formula used to calculate the incentive pay is</p>
        <p>{{ percentage_buyout_3 }}% + (Y% - {{ percentage_buyout_2 }}%)(0.2333) = Total Incentive Pay%</p>
        <p>where Y is the total % buyout.</p>
        <p>The maximum allowed Total Incentive Pay is {{ max_incentive_pay }}%.</p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Some hypothetical example calculations of faculty research incentive pay as Chih Loo would calculate them are listed below.</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Faculty</th>
                    <th>Buyout%</th>
                    <th>Research Incentive Pay from first 20% buyout</th>
                    <th>Research Incentive Pay from &gt;20% buyout</th>
                    <th>Total % Incentive Pay</th>
                    <th>May not exceed 14%</th>
                    <th>Course reduction</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for row in example_data %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ row.faculty_id }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row.buyout_percent }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ row.incentive_first_20 }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ row.incentive_over_20 }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ row.total_incentive }}%</td>
                    <td>{{ row.exceeds_14 }}</td>
                    <td>{{ row.course_reduction }}</td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>

    </div>
</body>
</html>